From 585253dc260f186b0d89badfd246286c65bf27ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:29:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250: add OnePlus sensor device
 info driver

The OnePlus SLPI firmware reads the sensor hardware description (sensor
type, bus, mount direction, calibration parameters) from SMEM item 130.
The bootloader only allocates the item; the downstream kernel fills it
from the device tree. Without it the DSP skips the accelerometer and the
magnetometer.

Add a small driver that fills SMEM item 130 from a "oneplus,sensor-devinfo"
DT node, its binding, and the node for instantnoodlep (values from the
vendor device tree, project 19811).

Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
---
